Subject: [PATCH] dispatch ready candidate queries without waiting for a radio tick

The controller admitted a fully prepared Unassociated STA Link Metrics
Query but only set its pending state. The radio's periodic timer then sent
it, adding up to one second to each serialized native query. Multiple bands
and eight-STA batches compounded that delay and aged other cached results.

Dispatch through the existing metrics state handler while the orchestrator
owns its recursive command lock. The normal timeout path takes the same
lock; the existing outstanding-MID guard prevents duplicate transmission.
Failed sends still retry on the normal timer. Reporting periods, response
deadlines and native single-flight admission are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/em/em.cpp
+++ b/src/em/em.cpp
@@ -284,6 +284,7 @@
 
         case em_cmd_type_unassoc_sta_query:
             m_sm.set_state(em_state_ctrl_unassoc_sta_link_metrics_pending);
+            em_metrics_t::process_ctrl_state();
             break;
 
 	default:
